```

Some could be real problems but most are not. Many warnings are for something like this:
```
char buf[HUGE_BUFFER_SIZE];
char temp[HUGE_BUFFER_SIZE];

strncpy(buf, HUGE_BUFFER_SIZE, <my input>);
snprintf(temp, HUGE_BUFFER_SIZE, "%s some trailer", buf); 
```
This will warn that truncation is possible (which is true), even if you know \<my input\> length can only be a small fraction of HUGE_BUFFER_SIZE. Maybe not the cleanest code in the world but it's not a real issue that needs fixing. But it's hard to tell without investigating each and every one. Writing code from scratch it's easier to avoid these issues. Fixing existing code is painful.

